## Attribution

- Contains data from Publisher car-availability.
- Contains data from Publisher electric-vehicle-chargers.
- Contains data from Publisher road-collisions.
- Contains data from Publisher travel-to-work.

## Core compatibility

This module is built against core \`atlas-core-1\` (the current key is \`atlas-core-1\`). It joins to the areas, releases and lookups in core, so use it only with a core carrying the same key.

## Using this module

The module database is \`sqlite/atlas-transport.sqlite\`. It is not built yet, so there is nothing to attach today (see Status).

SQLite attaches at most 10 extra databases to one connection by default, and the \`sqlite3\` command line and \`node:sqlite\` both use that limit. Raising it means recompiling SQLite. Attached databases also lose foreign keys across files, and a view or trigger in one file cannot refer to tables in another. To use several modules together, assemble core plus the modules you choose into one file, or read the per-module Parquet files with DuckDB, which has no such limit.
"
